  "worked_solution": "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nDividing both sides of the given inequality by ${2}^{3x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}-25)^{3}\\cdot {2}^{3x} & <0 \\\\ \\frac{({x}^{2}-25)^{3}\\cdot {2}^{3x}}{{2}^{3x}} & <\\frac{0}{{2}^{3x}} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-25)^{3} & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{({x}^{2}-25)^{3}} & <\\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ {x}^{2}-25 & <0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & <25 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & <\\sqrt{25} \\\\ |x| & <5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $-5<x<5.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
